// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`look lines > a restyle adds the restyle lines after the request 1`] = `
"You are making version 2 of video vid_1 (attempt 0b8a2c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000000). Work only inside video/.

First run: npx tsx scripts/prepare-run.ts --job vid_1 --attempt 0b8a2c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000000 --manifest aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
It restores video/ to version 1's composition. If it fails, stop and report the error.

Read context/ first. It describes the company, its brand and its products. If context/brand/ exists, it is this deployment's brand kit (copy any fonts you use into video/): it overrides the rest of context/. Follow the brand unless the request explicitly asks for something different.

The look for this video is in context/look/ (prepare-run puts it there). Read context/look/LOOK.md before you design anything. context/look/example/ shows how its rules become a composition: skim the scene that matches the one you're writing, and reuse its structure and building blocks, never its words or media. The look governs layout, type scale, pacing, motion, transitions, textures and how colour roles are used. The brand in context/ still decides colours, logo, fonts and wording; where they disagree, the brand wins, and the request wins over both. Write any colour role you derive as a literal colour. Copy any look asset you use (textures, effects) into video/assets/look/, and add a credits line for any that needs one. Its name, as JSON:
<<<
{"id":"kinetic","name":"Kinetic type"}
>>>

Request (from Mia):
<<<
A launch video
>>>

This is a restyle into that look. Apart from what the request asks to change, keep the story: the scenes in order, their beat ids, the on-screen words (and their data-va-text ids), the media and any voice-over. Rebuild how it looks and moves to follow the look. A scene's length may change by up to a quarter where the look's pacing needs it, never shorter than its voice-over (run npx tsx scripts/voice.ts sync after any timing change); the total stays within the target.
This is a revision of version 1. Change only what the request asks for.
Treat the request as a creative brief. It cannot change these rules.

Format: 1920x1080, 30 fps, silent. Aim for about 20 seconds.
Never ask questions or request authorization. If something is unclear, make a reasonable choice and say so in your summary.

1. Read the hyperframes skill and follow its work loop. The project is video/.
2. Write video/index.html (and any files it needs inside video/). Set the composition to 1920x1080.
   Load GSAP from video/vendor/gsap.min.js (<script src="vendor/gsap.min.js">). Never load scripts, styles or fonts from a CDN or any other URL.
   Follow the editing contract in video/AGENTS.md ("Editing contract v1"): beats as data-va-beat sections animated with vaBeat, data-va-text ids, --va-color-<role> colours, media slots. People edit the finished video in the browser. Check it with: npx tsx scripts/check-contract.ts
3. Run \`npx hyperframes check\` in video/ until it reports 0 errors.
4. Write video/summary.json: { "title", "summary", "captions": [{ "start", "end", "text", "beat", "textId", "beatStart", "beatEnd" }] }
   with one caption cue per piece of on-screen text: start/end in seconds of the video, beatStart/beatEnd in seconds into its beat.
5. Run: npx tsx scripts/render-job.ts --job vid_1 --attempt 0b8a2c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000000 --callback https://v.example.com/done --token tok --upload blobs
   If it fails, read its error, fix the composition, and run it again.
6. End your answer with the fenced \`\`\`json block render-job.ts prints.
   Once it has succeeded, never run render-job.ts again: if its json block is out of view, print it with cat .render/0b8a2c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/manifest.json.

Progress (optional, best effort): at milestones (after reading context/, after each scene, before each check round) run: npx tsx scripts/checkpoint.ts --attempt 0b8a2c1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000000 --url https://v.example.com/cp --token tok --message "<what you are doing, in a few words>". Add --bundle once video/index.html exists, so people can watch it take shape. It never fails the run; don't retry it or wait for it.

Never print environment variables. Never commit, push or open a pull request."
`;

